# Checks out the demo Customer's Cart against the compose stack (`docker compose up -d --build`), in
# two steps: a Checkout Session holds the Cart with every running Campaign's Discount, takes a
# Shipping address and a Shipping option, and may take a Coupon, then paying it buys it. Run the
# requests top to
# bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token request stores a token for the ones after it.
# Its client and webhook secrets are the stack's own: run it in the `dev` environment, whose
# http-client.private.env.json holds them (the root README's "Secrets" says how to write it).

@checkout = http://localhost:8086
@cart = http://localhost:8083
@orders = http://localhost:8085
@inventory = http://localhost:8082
@promotions = http://localhost:8087
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token

### Customer token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo&scope=openid

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff token, to set up a Coupon with a Usage limit and read its holds
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### An empty Cart can't be checked out: 400
DELETE {{cart}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Fill the Cart: two of one Pixel 9 Variant (Obsidian, 256 GB), by its Variant ID
PUT {{cart}}/cart/items/PHN-PIXEL-9-OBSIDIAN-256
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 2}

###
PUT {{cart}}/cart/items/AUD-JBL-FLIP-6
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 1}

### Stock before checkout
GET {{inventory}}/stock/PHN-PIXEL-9-OBSIDIAN-256

### Start checkout: 201 with the Checkout Session, priced from Catalog, held for 15 minutes. The
### seeded Audio week Campaign already takes 15% off the JBL speaker, the one audio line
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("sessionId", response.body.id); %}

### Two fewer available, as many on hand: a Reservation holds them
GET {{inventory}}/stock/PHN-PIXEL-9-OBSIDIAN-256

### The session, until it expires; 404 after
GET {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/current
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Starting again replaces it and releases its Reservation
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("sessionId", response.body.id); %}

### Apply the demo Coupon, in any case: Audio week's Discount, then WELCOME10's 10% off what is left
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "welcome10"}

### A Coupon that doesn't apply: 422 with Promotions' reason (unknown); the session keeps both Discounts
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "NO-SUCH-CODE"}

### Take the Coupon off: only Audio week's Discount is left
DELETE {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Coupon with one use in all (Staff, in Promotions)
POST {{promotions}}/coupons
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTP-ONCE", "discount": {"type": "PERCENT_OFF", "percentOff": 5},
 "validFrom": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "validUntil": "2030-01-01T00:00:00Z", "active": true, "usageLimit": 1}

### Applying it holds its one use for the session until the session expires
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "HTTP-ONCE"}

### It reads holds 1, state exhausted: another Customer applying it now gets 422 exhausted
GET {{promotions}}/coupons/HTTP-ONCE
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### And back on with WELCOME10, to pay with it: replacing HTTP-ONCE releases its hold
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "WELCOME10"}

### Paying before the session has a Shipping address and option: 409 shippingIncomplete
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentMethod": "tok_approve"}

### HTTP-ONCE reads holds 0, state active again; delete it
DELETE {{promotions}}/coupons/HTTP-ONCE
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A German address with a postcode in the wrong format: 422 invalidShippingAddress, naming it
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/shipping-address
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientName": "Demo Customer", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "1011", "city": "Berlin",
 "country": "DE"}

### A country the store doesn't ship to: 422 undeliverableCountry
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/shipping-address
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientName": "Demo Customer", "line1": "1 Main St", "postcode": "10001", "city": "New York",
 "country": "US"}

### A Dutch address, typed loosely: 200 with it normalised (1011 AB) and the options quoted for it,
### at domestic prices, since a Dutch address ships from the Amsterdam Warehouse
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/shipping-address
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientName": "  Demo   Customer ", "line1": "Damrak 1", "postcode": "1011ab",
 "city": "Amsterdam", "country": "nl"}

### An option that wasn't quoted: 422 shippingOptionNotQuoted
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/shipping-option
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"optionId": "OVERNIGHT"}

### Express: 200, its cost in shippingCost and the total, which the Discounts leave alone
PUT {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/shipping-option
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"optionId": "EXPRESS"}

### Pay with a declining test card: the checkout Saga's run ends DECLINED, a 402 with its
### declineReason; that Order is CANCELLED, and the run is in Temporal's UI (http://localhost:8233)
### under the session's ID
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentMethod": "tok_insufficient_funds"}

### The gateway fails to answer: the Saga tries 4 times over about 10 seconds, then cancels that
### Order too. Checkout waits 10 seconds, so this is a 502, or a 202 PROCESSING if it is still trying
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentMethod": "tok_gateway_error"}

### The latest attempt to pay the session: FAILED once the Saga gives up
GET {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/payment
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The session still holds the Cart, so it can be paid again
GET {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/current
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### No paymentMethod: 400, and nothing happens
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Pay with the approving test card: 200 with the Order in PAID, the Saga's new run
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentMethod": "tok_approve"}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.orderId); %}

### The Order, at the session's Prices, with Audio week's and WELCOME10's Discounts, its tax (zero for
### now), its Shipping address and Express option with its cost, and the total its Payment was for,
### every change by ORCHESTRATION
GET {{orders}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Two fewer on hand now: the Reservation was committed
GET {{inventory}}/stock/PHN-PIXEL-9-OBSIDIAN-256

### The latest attempt still answers once the session is over: PAID, with the Order
GET {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/payment
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Cart is empty again, and the session is over: 404
GET {{cart}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sessionId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentMethod": "tok_approve"}

### More than there is in stock: 409 naming the Variant, and no session
PUT {{cart}}/cart/items/PHN-PIXEL-9
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 10000}

###
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Without a token: 401
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions

### Orchestration token: the checkout Saga's own identity, for the commands it calls
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=orchestration&client_secret={{orchestrationClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("orchestrationToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The demo Customer's ID: the sub Orchestration names in the body
GET http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.sub); %}

### Fill the Cart and start a session for the Saga to end
PUT {{cart}}/cart/items/PHN-PIXEL-9-OBSIDIAN-256
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 1}

###
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("sagaSessionId", response.body.id); %}

### Orchestration ends it: 204; sending it again is the same 204
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sagaSessionId}}/end
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### The session is over: 404
GET {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/current
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Customer can't end a session this way: 403
POST {{checkout}}/checkout/sessions/{{sagaSessionId}}/end
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}
